('nabteb','157498ec-9692-44b7-a733-02b697336f85'::uuid,'Grammar & Structure','Choose the correct preposition: I agree ___ your suggestion.','[{"id":"A","text":"from"},{"id":"B","text":"with"},{"id":"C","text":"to"},{"id":"D","text":"for"}]'::jsonb,'B','The standard combination is agree with.','medium','Cambridge / British Council / Purdue grammar references','https://dictionary.cambridge.org/us/grammar/british-grammar/present-perfect-simple-i-','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('nabteb','157498ec-9692-44b7-a733-02b697336f85'::uuid,'Grammar & Structure','Choose the correct preposition: She listens ___ the radio.','[{"id":"A","text":"to"},{"id":"B","text":"at"},{"id":"C","text":"for"},{"id":"D","text":"with"}]'::jsonb,'A','The standard verb-preposition combination is listen to.','medium','Cambridge / British Council / Purdue grammar references','https://dictionary.cambridge.org/us/grammar/british-grammar/present-perfect-simple-i-','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('nabteb','157498ec-9692-44b7-a733-02b697336f85'::uuid,'Grammar & Structure','Choose the correct preposition: They are waiting ___ the bus.','[{"id":"A","text":"to"},{"id":"B","text":"with"},{"id":"C","text":"of"},{"id":"D","text":"for"}]'::jsonb,'D','The standard combination is wait for.','medium','Cambridge / British Council / Purdue grammar references','https://dictionary.cambridge.org/us/grammar/british-grammar/present-perfect-simple-i-','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('nabteb','157498ec-9692-44b7-a733-02b697336f85'::uuid,'Grammar & Structure','Choose the correct pronoun: The teacher spoke to Ada and ___.','[{"id":"A","text":"they"},{"id":"B","text":"me"},{"id":"C","text":"I"},{"id":"D","text":"we"}]'::jsonb,'B','The pronoun is the object of the preposition to, so objective case me is correct.','medium','Cambridge / British Council / Purdue grammar references','https://dictionary.cambridge.org/us/grammar/british-grammar/present-perfect-simple-i-','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('nabteb','157498ec-9692-44b7-a733-02b697336f85'::uuid,'Grammar & Structure','Choose the correct sentence about one item.','[{"id":"A","text":"One of the books are missing."},{"id":"B","text":"One of the books be missing."},{"id":"C","text":"One of the books were missing now."},{"id":"D","text":"One of the books is missing."}]'::jsonb,'D','The head subject one is singular, so is agrees with it.','medium','Cambridge / British Council / Purdue grammar references','https://dictionary.cambridge.org/us/grammar/british-grammar/present-perfect-simple-i-','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('nabteb','157498ec-9692-44b7-a733-02b697336f85'::uuid,'Grammar & Structure','Choose the correct sentence for a plural subject.','[{"id":"A","text":"The students are ready."},{"id":"B","text":"The students is ready."},{"id":"C","text":"The students am ready."},{"id":"D","text":"The students be ready."}]'::jsonb,'A','The plural subject students agrees with are.','medium','Cambridge / British Council / Purdue grammar references','https://dictionary.cambridge.org/us/grammar/british-grammar/present-perfect-simple-i-','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('nabteb','157498ec-9692-44b7-a733-02b697336f85'::uuid,'Grammar & Structure','Choose the correct sentence.','[{"id":"A","text":"She finishing has her work."},{"id":"B","text":"She has finished her work."},{"id":"C","text":"She have finished her work."},{"id":"D","text":"She has finish her work."}]'::jsonb,'B','The present perfect uses has/have plus the past participle.','medium','Cambridge / British Council / Purdue grammar references','https://dictionary.cambridge.org/us/grammar/british-grammar/present-perfect-simple-i-','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('nabteb','157498ec-9692-44b7-a733-02b697336f85'::uuid,'Grammar & Structure','Choose the correct subject-verb agreement.','[{"id":"A","text":"The boys plays football."},{"id":"B","text":"The boy playing football."},{"id":"C","text":"The boy plays football."},{"id":"D","text":"The boy play football."}]'::jsonb,'C','A singular third-person subject takes plays in the simple present.','medium','Cambridge / British Council / Purdue grammar references','https://dictionary.cambridge.org/us/grammar/british-grammar/present-perfect-simple-i-','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('nabteb','157498ec-9692-44b7-a733-02b697336f85'::uuid,'Grammar & Structure','Which form is a present perfect question?','[{"id":"A","text":"Have you finished?"},{"id":"B","text":"Did you finished?"},{"id":"C","text":"Do you have finished?"},{"id":"D","text":"Are you finish?"}]'::jsonb,'A','Present perfect questions use have/has plus the past participle.','medium','Cambridge / British Council / Purdue grammar references','https://dictionary.cambridge.org/us/grammar/british-grammar/present-perfect-simple-i-','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('nabteb','157498ec-9692-44b7-a733-02b697336f85'::uuid,'Grammar & Structure','Which phrase correctly uses for to express duration?','[{"id":"A","text":"for 2020"},{"id":"B","text":"for last Monday"},{"id":"C","text":"for yesterday"},{"id":"D","text":"for three years"}]'::jsonb,'D','For is used for a period or duration.','medium','Cambridge / British Council / Purdue grammar references','https://dictionary.cambridge.org/us/grammar/british-grammar/present-perfect-simple-i-','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('nabteb','157498ec-9692-44b7-a733-02b697336f85'::uuid,'Grammar & Structure','Which phrase correctly uses since?','[{"id":"A","text":"since 2020"},{"id":"B","text":"since three years"},{"id":"C","text":"since two hours"},{"id":"D","text":"since several months"}]'::jsonb,'A','Since refers to a point in time.','medium','Cambridge / British Council / Purdue grammar references','https://dictionary.cambridge.org/us/grammar/british-grammar/present-perfect-simple-i-','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('nabteb','157498ec-9692-44b7-a733-02b697336f85'::uuid,'Grammar & Structure','Which pronoun is in the possessive case?','[{"id":"A","text":"they"},{"id":"B","text":"who"},{"id":"C","text":"theirs"},{"id":"D","text":"them"}]'::jsonb,'C','Theirs expresses possession.','medium','Cambridge / British Council / Purdue grammar references','https://dictionary.cambridge.org/us/grammar/british-grammar/present-perfect-simple-i-','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('nabteb','157498ec-9692-44b7-a733-02b697336f85'::uuid,'Grammar & Structure','Which sentence correctly uses the present perfect?','[{"id":"A","text":"I lived here since 2021 and still do."},{"id":"B","text":"I have lived here since 2021."},{"id":"C","text":"I live here since 2021."},{"id":"D","text":"I am living here since 2021."}]'::jsonb,'B','Present perfect is used for a situation that began in the past and continues to the present.','medium','Cambridge / British Council / Purdue grammar references','https://dictionary.cambridge.org/us/grammar/british-grammar/present-perfect-simple-i-','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('nabteb','157498ec-9692-44b7-a733-02b697336f85'::uuid,'Grammar & Structure','Which sentence uses yet naturally with the present perfect?','[{"id":"A","text":"I didn''t finished yet."},{"id":"B","text":"I am not finish yet."},{"id":"C","text":"I have finish yesterday."},{"id":"D","text":"I haven''t finished yet."}]'::jsonb,'D','Yet commonly appears in present-perfect negatives and questions.','medium','Cambridge / British Council / Purdue grammar references','https://dictionary.cambridge.org/us/grammar/british-grammar/present-perfect-simple-i-','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('nabteb','157498ec-9692-44b7-a733-02b697336f85'::uuid,'Grammar & Structure','Which tense is most suitable for a completed action at a definite past time such as yesterday?','[{"id":"A","text":"Future perfect"},{"id":"B","text":"Present continuous"},{"id":"C","text":"Past simple"},{"id":"D","text":"Present perfect"}]'::jsonb,'C','Past simple is normally used for a definite completed past time.','medium','Cambridge / British Council / Purdue grammar references','https://dictionary.cambridge.org/us/grammar/british-grammar/present-perfect-simple-i-','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('nabteb','22f09930-c43f-4b8b-bec2-a2fa667b7a99'::uuid,'Cybersecurity','A fake website designed to imitate a trusted login page is commonly used in:','[{"id":"A","text":"Phishing"},{"id":"B","text":"Defragmentation"},{"id":"C","text":"Spreadsheet formatting"},{"id":"D","text":"Image rendering"}]'::jsonb,'A','Phishing often uses fake websites that imitate trusted services.','medium','NIST Cybersecurity and Privacy','https://www.nist.gov/cybersecurity-and-privacy/how-do-i-create-good-password','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('nabteb','22f09930-c43f-4b8b-bec2-a2fa667b7a99'::uuid,'Cybersecurity','A second authentication factor is valuable because it:','[{"id":"A","text":"Makes every password public"},{"id":"B","text":"Removes the need for identity checks"},{"id":"C","text":"Disables account security"},{"id":"D","text":"Adds another proof of identity"}]'::jsonb,'D','A second factor adds another layer of identity verification.','medium','NIST Cybersecurity and Privacy','https://www.nist.gov/cybersecurity-and-privacy/how-do-i-create-good-password','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('nabteb','22f09930-c43f-4b8b-bec2-a2fa667b7a99'::uuid,'Cybersecurity','If an attacker obtains an offline copy of password hashes, why is password strength important?','[{"id":"A","text":"Attackers can make many guesses without normal login-page limits"},{"id":"B","text":"The monitor becomes damaged"},{"id":"C","text":"The account changes owner automatically"},{"id":"D","text":"The keyboard is disabled"}]'::jsonb,'A','Offline guessing can allow very large numbers of password guesses.','medium','NIST Cybersecurity and Privacy','https://www.nist.gov/cybersecurity-and-privacy/how-do-i-create-good-password','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('nabteb','22f09930-c43f-4b8b-bec2-a2fa667b7a99'::uuid,'Cybersecurity','What is phishing?','[{"id":"A","text":"A method of compressing files"},{"id":"B","text":"A type of printer"},{"id":"C","text":"A database backup process"},{"id":"D","text":"A trick that attempts to make a user reveal credentials or sensitive information"}]'::jsonb,'D','NIST describes phishing as tricking users into giving away credentials or information.','medium','NIST Cybersecurity and Privacy','https://www.nist.gov/cybersecurity-and-privacy/how-do-i-create-good-password','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('nabteb','22f09930-c43f-4b8b-bec2-a2fa667b7a99'::uuid,'Cybersecurity','What is the main purpose of authentication?','[{"id":"A","text":"To compress documents"},{"id":"B","text":"To sort files alphabetically"},{"id":"C","text":"To verify identity before granting access"},{"id":"D","text":"To increase screen resolution"}]'::jsonb,'C','Authentication verifies a user''s identity before access is granted.','medium','NIST Cybersecurity and Privacy','https://www.nist.gov/cybersecurity-and-privacy/how-do-i-create-good-password','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('nabteb','22f09930-c43f-4b8b-bec2-a2fa667b7a99'::uuid,'Cybersecurity','Which action is safest after receiving a suspicious login link?','[{"id":"A","text":"Forward your password to the sender"},{"id":"B","text":"Disable browser security warnings"},{"id":"C","text":"Avoid entering credentials and verify the site independently"},{"id":"D","text":"Enter the password quickly"}]'::jsonb,'C','Suspicious links can be phishing attempts; credentials should not be entered without verification.','medium','NIST Cybersecurity and Privacy','https://www.nist.gov/cybersecurity-and-privacy/how-do-i-create-good-password','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('nabteb','22f09930-c43f-4b8b-bec2-a2fa667b7a99'::uuid,'Cybersecurity','Which attack relies heavily on social engineering to steal passwords?','[{"id":"A","text":"Disk partitioning"},{"id":"B","text":"Phishing"},{"id":"C","text":"File indexing"},{"id":"D","text":"Data sorting"}]'::jsonb,'B','Phishing is a common social-engineering route for credential theft.','medium','NIST Cybersecurity and Privacy','https://www.nist.gov/cybersecurity-and-privacy/how-do-i-create-good-password','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('nabteb','22f09930-c43f-4b8b-bec2-a2fa667b7a99'::uuid,'Cybersecurity','Which credential choice is especially poor security practice?','[{"id":"A","text":"Checking a site address"},{"id":"B","text":"Using 12345 as a password"},{"id":"C","text":"Using a unique password"},{"id":"D","text":"Using multifactor authentication"}]'::jsonb,'B','NIST highlights common passwords such as 12345 as weak choices.','medium','NIST Cybersecurity and Privacy','https://www.nist.gov/cybersecurity-and-privacy/how-do-i-create-good-password','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('nabteb','22f09930-c43f-4b8b-bec2-a2fa667b7a99'::uuid,'Cybersecurity','Which practice is safer for separate online accounts?','[{"id":"A","text":"Use the same short password"},{"id":"B","text":"Publish passwords in notes online"},{"id":"C","text":"Turn off all authentication"},{"id":"D","text":"Use unique passwords"}]'::jsonb,'D','Unique passwords limit the damage from credential compromise.','medium','NIST Cybersecurity and Privacy','https://www.nist.gov/cybersecurity-and-privacy/how-do-i-create-good-password','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('nabteb','22f09930-c43f-4b8b-bec2-a2fa667b7a99'::uuid,'Cybersecurity','Which step improves account security beyond relying only on a password?','[{"id":"A","text":"Sharing passwords with friends"},{"id":"B","text":"Disabling login alerts"},{"id":"C","text":"Using multifactor authentication"},{"id":"D","text":"Reusing the same password everywhere"}]'::jsonb,'C','NIST recommends stronger authentication such as multifactor authentication.','medium','NIST Cybersecurity and Privacy','https://www.nist.gov/cybersecurity-and-privacy/how-do-i-create-good-password','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('nabteb','22f09930-c43f-4b8b-bec2-a2fa667b7a99'::uuid,'Cybersecurity','Why can very simple passwords be unsafe?','[{"id":"A","text":"They may be easy for attackers to guess"},{"id":"B","text":"They always damage hardware"},{"id":"C","text":"They prevent internet access"},{"id":"D","text":"They encrypt files automatically"}]'::jsonb,'A','NIST warns that common passwords are easy for attackers to guess.','medium','NIST Cybersecurity and Privacy','https://www.nist.gov/cybersecurity-and-privacy/how-do-i-create-good-password','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('nabteb','22f09930-c43f-4b8b-bec2-a2fa667b7a99'::uuid,'Cybersecurity','Why is reusing the same password on many sites risky?','[{"id":"A","text":"It changes file formats"},{"id":"B","text":"A breach on one site can threaten other accounts using the same password"},{"id":"C","text":"It makes monitors brighter"},{"id":"D","text":"It slows internet speed"}]'::jsonb,'B','Password reuse can let one breached credential compromise multiple accounts.','medium','NIST Cybersecurity and Privacy','https://www.nist.gov/cybersecurity-and-privacy/how-do-i-create-good-password','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('nabteb','32929c31-b38c-4e52-8214-b656cca924b0'::uuid,'Business Finance','A vehicle used to operate a business and not held for sale is normally what type of asset?','[{"id":"A","text":"Revenue item"},{"id":"B","text":"Dividend"},{"id":"C","text":"Noncurrent/fixed asset"},{"id":"D","text":"Current liability"}]'::jsonb,'C','Operational vehicles are generally fixed/noncurrent assets.','medium','U.S. SEC Beginner''s Guide to Financial Statements','https://www.sec.gov/files/investor/pubs/begfinstmtguide.htm','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('nabteb','32929c31-b38c-4e52-8214-b656cca924b0'::uuid,'Business Finance','After liabilities are deducted from assets, the remaining owners'' interest is called what?','[{"id":"A","text":"Gross sales"},{"id":"B","text":"Equity"},{"id":"C","text":"Revenue"},{"id":"D","text":"Inventory"}]'::jsonb,'B','Equity is the residual interest after liabilities.','medium','U.S. SEC Beginner''s Guide to Financial Statements','https://www.sec.gov/files/investor/pubs/begfinstmtguide.htm','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('nabteb','32929c31-b38c-4e52-8214-b656cca924b0'::uuid,'Business Finance','For a business, cash is generally classified as what?','[{"id":"A","text":"A liability"},{"id":"B","text":"An expense only"},{"id":"C","text":"A dividend"},{"id":"D","text":"An asset"}]'::jsonb,'D','Cash is an asset.','medium','U.S. SEC Beginner''s Guide to Financial Statements','https://www.sec.gov/files/investor/pubs/begfinstmtguide.htm','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('nabteb','32929c31-b38c-4e52-8214-b656cca924b0'::uuid,'Business Finance','For a trading business, unsold inventory is normally classified as what?','[{"id":"A","text":"A liability"},{"id":"B","text":"A dividend"},{"id":"C","text":"A tax"},{"id":"D","text":"An asset"}]'::jsonb,'D','Inventory is an asset.','medium','U.S. SEC Beginner''s Guide to Financial Statements','https://www.sec.gov/files/investor/pubs/begfinstmtguide.htm','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('nabteb','32929c31-b38c-4e52-8214-b656cca924b0'::uuid,'Business Finance','In business finance, which equation must a balance sheet satisfy?','[{"id":"A","text":"Revenue = Assets + Cash"},{"id":"B","text":"Assets = Revenue - Expenses"},{"id":"C","text":"Liabilities = Cash + Sales"},{"id":"D","text":"Assets = Liabilities + Shareholders'' Equity"}]'::jsonb,'D','A balance sheet follows Assets = Liabilities + Shareholders'' Equity.','medium','U.S. SEC Beginner''s Guide to Financial Statements','https://www.sec.gov/files/investor/pubs/begfinstmtguide.htm','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('nabteb','32929c31-b38c-4e52-8214-b656cca924b0'::uuid,'Business Finance','Money a business owes to a supplier is generally classified as what?','[{"id":"A","text":"A dividend"},{"id":"B","text":"Revenue"},{"id":"C","text":"A liability"},{"id":"D","text":"An asset"}]'::jsonb,'C','Amounts owed to suppliers are liabilities.','medium','U.S. SEC Beginner''s Guide to Financial Statements','https://www.sec.gov/files/investor/pubs/begfinstmtguide.htm','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('nabteb','32929c31-b38c-4e52-8214-b656cca924b0'::uuid,'Business Finance','Which classification normally applies to an asset expected to turn into cash within a year?','[{"id":"A","text":"Current asset"},{"id":"B","text":"Long-term liability"},{"id":"C","text":"Equity reserve"},{"id":"D","text":"Revenue"}]'::jsonb,'A','Such an item is generally a current asset.','medium','U.S. SEC Beginner''s Guide to Financial Statements','https://www.sec.gov/files/investor/pubs/begfinstmtguide.htm','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('nabteb','32929c31-b38c-4e52-8214-b656cca924b0'::uuid,'Business Finance','Which statement focuses on cash moving into and out of a company?','[{"id":"A","text":"Cash flow statement"},{"id":"B","text":"Balance sheet only"},{"id":"C","text":"Sales invoice"},{"id":"D","text":"Share certificate"}]'::jsonb,'A','The cash flow statement reports cash inflows and outflows.','medium','U.S. SEC Beginner''s Guide to Financial Statements','https://www.sec.gov/files/investor/pubs/begfinstmtguide.htm','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('nabteb','32929c31-b38c-4e52-8214-b656cca924b0'::uuid,'Business Finance','Which statement is most useful for reviewing revenue and expenses over a period?','[{"id":"A","text":"Purchase order"},{"id":"B","text":"Income statement"},{"id":"C","text":"Balance sheet"},{"id":"D","text":"Share certificate"}]'::jsonb,'B','An income statement reports revenues and expenses over a period.','medium','U.S. SEC Beginner''s Guide to Financial Statements','https://www.sec.gov/files/investor/pubs/begfinstmtguide.htm','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('nabteb','32929c31-b38c-4e52-8214-b656cca924b0'::uuid,'Business Finance','Which statement is used to view a company''s financial position at one date?','[{"id":"A","text":"Cash flow statement"},{"id":"B","text":"Sales invoice"},{"id":"C","text":"Balance sheet"},{"id":"D","text":"Income statement"}]'::jsonb,'C','A balance sheet shows financial position at a point in time.','medium','U.S. SEC Beginner''s Guide to Financial Statements','https://www.sec.gov/files/investor/pubs/begfinstmtguide.htm','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
