('nabteb','7f8c838f-1e73-4098-b6db-f6e3dbbf2ea3'::uuid,'Ohm''s Law','A current of 0.25 A flows through a 40 Ω resistor. What is the voltage across it?','[{"id":"A","text":"10 V"},{"id":"B","text":"50 V"},{"id":"C","text":"20 V"},{"id":"D","text":"5 V"}]'::jsonb,'A','Using V = IR, V = 0.25 × 40 = 10 V.','medium','NASA Ohm''s Law','https://www.nasa.gov/stem-content/ohms-law/','authoritative-web+deterministic',now(),true,now()),
('nabteb','7f8c838f-1e73-4098-b6db-f6e3dbbf2ea3'::uuid,'Ohm''s Law','A current of 0.5 A flows through a 20 Ω resistor. What is the voltage across it?','[{"id":"A","text":"30 V"},{"id":"B","text":"20 V"},{"id":"C","text":"5 V"},{"id":"D","text":"10 V"}]'::jsonb,'D','Using V = IR, V = 0.5 × 20 = 10 V.','medium','NASA Ohm''s Law','https://www.nasa.gov/stem-content/ohms-law/','authoritative-web+deterministic',now(),true,now()),
